{"step_index":453,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T22:09:44Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-09T06:09:44+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-09T06:09:47+08:00\nThe search for \"prevent long press select all text selection mobile web ios android -webkit-touch-callout user-select\" returned the following summary:\nTo completely prevent long-press context menus, text highlighting, and \"select all\" behaviors on mobile web (iOS Safari and Android Chrome/Firefox), you need a combination of **CSS properties** and sometimes **JavaScript touch/contextmenu event prevention**.\n\n### 1. The CSS Solution (Recommended)\n\nApply these styles to the specific elements (like buttons, images, or UI components) or globally to your app wrapper[1]:\n\n```css\n.no-select {\n  /* Standard property supported by modern browsers */\n  user-select: none;\n  \n  /* Prevent iOS Safari text selection and default callout popup menu */\n  -webkit-user-select: none;\n  -webkit-touch-callout: none;\n  \n  /* Legacy prefixes for older mobile browsers */\n  -khtml-user-select: none;\n  -moz-user-select: none;\n  -ms-user-select: none;\n  \n  /* Removes the grey/blue tap highlight box on mobile webkit */\n  -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent;\n}\n```\n\n* **`user-select: none;`**: Stops text from being highlighted or selected[2][1].\n* **`-webkit-touch-callout: none;`**: Crucial for iOS. This specifically kills the popup menu/callout bubble that appears on a long-press (e.g., \"Copy\", \"Look Up\", \"Share\")[3][1].\n\n---\n\n### 2. The JavaScript Fallback (For Stubborn Long-Press Behaviors)\n\nSometimes on mobile browsers (particularly Android WebViews or specific iOS contexts), a long-press will still trigger selection handles or context menus. You can intercept and cancel these gestures via JavaScript:\n\n```javascript\n// Prevent context menu (long-press popup on desktop & mobile)\ndocument.addEventListener('contextmenu', function (e) {\n  e.preventDefault();\n});\n\n// Alternatively, target specific elements:\nconst element = document.querySelector('.no-select');\n\nelement.addEventListener('contextmenu', (e) => {\n  e.preventDefault();\n});\n```\n\nIf you want to prevent touch-hold behaviors entirely on a custom interactive component, you can also prevent default behavior on touch events, though use this cautiously as it can break scrolling if applied too broadly:\n\n```javascript\nelement.addEventListener('touchstart', function(e) {\n  // Use cautiously; prevents default touch actions like text grabbing\n  // Note: Avoid putting this on scrollable containers.\n}, { passive: false });\n```\n\nSources:\n[1] [flaviocopes.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE3LIzGMBEqk2RAi0oR9gS_9-RP6_wBKsk-t_ebxCLQD0X8Z8ac0qGMlt3NwOGucwVQMhAVw6us0qzx7uaHxxo2tpiWqmgTSRapBZzeJP7cCao0PiUtsaB58YPxFj8v1OGAjzlfuJuG2w==)\n[2] [fdgweb.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE2K7x5PmEmJHrbQOAgfzgcV3QYH8U3CegcgKJtZ-_lgk1_7utcYjS980acGUyB-OXmA9Ws3yemPT1GvapRW2YM_hqddtCZB_QQ5ueNXAWwwbTihao9Rz5l4umMauyK1Kzn1G2P8vPZBtBpofMwKOpEv3GapjO6E4uSKlhFiVOBw6SyQbLoiZLm-WK2rF7nrQJdow==)\n[3] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHmhAw4_5jpW3Q5E10SG3zsJH_kx_HGfRQQPGw0zreFEveqFmG0ToF1WQXpr2Mpaliv7_kMCm3HHJDBFn8c_HiuyHhUfXyTKf9txSCZQguChNzpJhSyZfO1cXPn5i-NBzGyT4h5UQSu)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link."}
{"step_index":454,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T22:09:47Z","input_tokens":2667,"cache_read_tokens":57860,"output_tokens":53,"tool_calls":[{"name":"search_web","args":{"query":"prevent ctrl a select all copy selectstart javascript web"}}]}
{"step_index":455,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T22:09:51Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-09T06:09:51+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-09T06:09:54+08:00\nThe search for \"prevent ctrl a select all copy selectstart javascript web\" returned the following summary:\nTo prevent users from selecting text, using **Ctrl+A** (Select All), copying content, or triggering selection events on a webpage, you can combine **CSS user-select** rules with **JavaScript event listeners**[1][2][3]. \n\nHere is the complete implementation approach:\n\n### 1. CSS (The Cleanest Way to Stop Text Selection & `selectstart`)\nThe easiest way to block highlighting and the `selectstart` behavior natively across elements is using `user-select`[1][4].\n\n```css\n.unselectable {\n  -webkit-user-select: none; /* Safari */\n  -moz-user-select: none;    /* Firefox */\n  -ms-user-select: none;     /* Internet Explorer/Edge */\n  user-select: none;         /* Standard syntax */\n}\n```\nYou can apply this globally to the `<body>` tag if you want to restrict selection across the entire page[1][4].\n\n---\n\n### 2. JavaScript (To Block Shortcuts like Ctrl+A and Copy Events)\nTo explicitly intercept keyboard shortcuts like **Ctrl+A** (or `Cmd+A` on Mac), block the `copy` event[5], and stop native selection (`selectstart`), use the following script:\n\n```javascript\ndocument.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {\n\n  // 1. Prevent Ctrl+A (Select All) and Ctrl+C (Copy) shortcuts\n  document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {\n    // Check for 'Ctrl' (or 'Cmd' on Mac via metaKey)\n    const isCtrl = e.ctrlKey || e.metaKey;\n\n    if (isCtrl && (e.key === 'a' || e.key === 'A' || e.key === 'c' || e.key === 'C')) {\n      e.preventDefault();\n      // Optional: console.log(\"Action blocked\");\n    }\n  });\n\n  // 2. Prevent the native copy event mechanism\n  document.addEventListener('copy', (e) => {\n    e.preventDefault();\n  });\n\n  // 3. Prevent text selection start events (covers legacy and direct drag selections)\n  document.addEventListener('selectstart', (e) => {\n    e.preventDefault();\n  });\n  \n});\n```\n\n### Important Caveat\nWhile these methods make casual copying and text highlighting difficult, **they are not foolproof**[6][7]. Tech-savvy users can easily bypass client-side JavaScript or CSS restrictions by disabling JavaScript in their browser settings, inspecting the page source/DOM, or reading data through browser developer tools.\n\nSources:\n[1] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEhawfF8YzMrbqREsaQC-nkJe-6mqj8E16q5BRyBgy-nulfezTf7WmjJHrh4C0wLK_K6DxsM4WcK_-XxlVEf4mYDUXKVTGrzZ9PhgfpFbqA9gvR8AhCHQlomF6nExG2_4ZQJfazo7CLRvtLTawE-09DE-86k0jtlAXEZ04=)\n[2] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGxi_HdTZ1_dzOog5hLxESgUPrGpySIRPwIfu26vf3Y4k3rngl9A_VTQctV227NNckAKMgtwO3J1Z9o0Vs_SjKKAykcUPpajoCKaEXOmSw6ZasG43spqjZTX8avIVJFdKw5iUs1FgEqHAsWroZ2R_Sw69xMg-l099HigkSpsmFvrV5XbZSGQoCGzrWq2ThzRKQwlJZa2l4ZEMu9TEiGhw==)\n[3] [html-code-generator.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFgtES7TWsXBsioIsRviv00hdtR8-UtOTJ9VIj0jcrp3uEFR0REQA8mJ1Qwij7oKFMH-WsoAuIDpWOz2YM3FYX4KaLeoFjwek6KL5L5ypF8iEaswgbAJyUs5BZI30rWYaYICGugUhHptIfSLpqiKtXh8NZayCiSxgoGQ-4W6MpS9Bc=)\n[4] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEz3HqTmQcwTpKu0eiXW0ydy5zsA3rPuy6hosj6xpnD6cupLAV0vIZguv23KhE_S_a5VzT-LVdLBxTu_Z0cIOSWO325-6GrgK9PCoiq2qeT0350JF5KZFEnwz_evpfouQGPlBpXzFSJpa1y5Q2RpFng8OvChAX2iutQw2fq8caPOPDjzPIcrFp5KV1o4rhs-F4=)\n[5] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGHsFcy3PiQ_Y4NVizHaVxi4UoL_-UST9O_IjhbMVUdW6y3THtImig7JQUf6a-0WxaeSEq0RrNkVyY2wqW9cPafJw13fU5NYRmin2h1L_0pZY48N6rH1XmXPco5FAJxzWkUZ4458mx4u39LGgfdIV9Vjoh7L6DX218ufp-DERKHfScTCiBx4lY=)\n[6] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFmu5Mc34JgULVH-xRuzsIqclrg8nVPAWlbEXNcKlA3s3doyKHk6gA8xzkZHIum5No2LV8hTLrlllWupp3CQa7JVLGgniWhMJI3XhaeRvrSdu97E4dj6nB1m7HQHtbpPRyjeEU44XEmR6KFbQai1oz_0Ua3p9nDM5et6IbUNb0x5iRco0s8S8opD0sqhVMLTraD0YpdFXsY)\n[7] [coreui.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH4RYd_mOc0f51t1fDpWjSVdutTbpk7L8JykP6vECN-WCHfuVSgYVeXDN2uuzrPLP9F1DPwPoBDhlcBQ29WgGjjGGch33CNvkYTegg3QUtR-iXsLZhR_WcwqnfCmbI5j3hUdLwLnQ4oB9DzphUF95BLKnnajUoc1IQ7lYbR9gaMm1gKXnmzEg==)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link."}
{"step_index":456,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T22:09:54Z","input_tokens":3009,"cache_read_tokens":59415,"output_tokens":3305,"thinking":"The task involves UI updates for teacher and student interfaces. Specifically, the \"Download QUIZ Json\" button label on the teacher interface needs to be updated. Simultaneously, the goal is to prevent text selection on the student interface across both mobile and desktop. Now the task focuses on disabling text selection on the student interface to prevent text grabbing.\n\n\nInvestigating methods to disable text selection on the student interface, considering the `contextmenu` event and associated behaviors like selection handles. Initial approach utilizes CSS properties `user-select: none` to prevent text selection across the body. However, concerns arise regarding input elements requiring user interaction; the CSS solution could interfere with the student's ability to input or edit text, specifically on mobile.\n\nTherefore, an adjustment is needed to ensure inputs and textareas retain their default `user-select: auto` property. JavaScript event listeners will be implemented to specifically block context menus, and selection start events on the document, but only for elements other than inputs and textareas.\n\n\nImplementing event listeners to prevent default actions for context menu and selection start events on the document, excluding input and textarea elements. Addressing keyboard shortcuts for \"select all\" and \"copy\" using `keydown` event listener, also excluding inputs and textareas. Considering potential issues with long-press gestures on mobile, investigating and applying specific CSS properties to disable context menus and selection handles across mobile platforms. Revisiting the result code copy button to ensure its functionality remains intact after disabling text selection.\n\n\nImplemented JavaScript event listeners and CSS properties to disable text selection on the student interface while ensuring text input elements remain functional. Addressing potential workarounds like keyboard shortcuts and mobile long-press gestures, confirming these methods are blocked. Confirmed that programmatic clipboard write using `navigator.clipboard.writeText()` is not affected by the added event listeners. Ensuring that the Firestore template for downloaded quizzes is updated to include the latest anti-selection measures.\n\n\nVerifying the latest changes require adding a new entry to `HISTORY.md` for the patch. The entry will document the text-selection disable features with an explanation. Rule 3 necessitates a verification plan; this plan will outline the affected files, components, and behaviors, specifying test cases to ensure continued functionality. Rule 5 guides the initial planning phase, ensuring the changes are correctly documented before implementation.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":true,"Summary":"Implementation plan to update teacher download button label to 'Download Quiz File' and block long-press, select-all, text selection, and context menus in index.html while preserving input field usability.","UserFacing":true},"Content":"# Implementation Plan: Block Long-Press Selection & Update Download Button Label\n\n## 1. Overview of Requested Changes\n\n1. **Button Label Update in [teacher.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html)**:\n   - Change the button text from `Download QUIZ Json` to **`Download Quiz File`**.\n   - Keep all existing download functionality (fetching template from Firestore `quizzes/template` with fallback to local `index.html`).\n\n2. **Block Long-Press & Select-All in [index.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html)**:\n   - Prevent mobile users from long-pressing to trigger context menus, text selection handles, magnifying callouts, and floating action menus (\"Select All\", \"Copy\", \"Share\", \"Web Search\").\n   - Prevent desktop/laptop users from highlighting text or using keyboard shortcuts like `Ctrl+A` / `Cmd+A` (Select All) or `Ctrl+C` / `Cmd+C` (Copy) outside input elements.\n   - **Crucial Usability Guard**: Must preserve normal focus, typing, text editing, and cursor navigation within student text inputs (`#name`, `#sec`, and any fallback textarea like `#codebox`).\n\n3. **Synchronize Firestore Template**:\n   - Update `quizzes/template` in Firestore so that any teacher downloading via `Download Quiz File` gets the updated `index.html` with the long-press and select-all protection.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Proposed Technical Implementation\n\n### 2.1 [teacher.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html)\n- Update line 116 button label:\n  `<button id=\"dl-quiz-btn\" class=\"sec\" type=\"button\">Download Quiz File</button>`\n\n### 2.2 [index.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html)\n- **CSS Enhancements**:\n  - Add global anti-selection and touch callout styles to `body`:\n    ```css\n    body {\n      -webkit-touch-callout: none;\n      -webkit-user-select: none;\n      -moz-user-select: none;\n      -ms-user-select: none;\n      user-select: none;\n    }\n    ```\n  - Ensure student inputs retain selection and editing capabilities:\n    ```css\n    input, textarea {\n      -webkit-user-select: auto;\n      user-select: auto;\n    }\n    ```\n- **JavaScript Event Interceptions**:\n  - Block `contextmenu` (long-press popups on mobile, right-click on desktop) unless target is an input or textarea:\n    ```javascript\n    document.addEventListener('contextmenu', e => {\n      if (e.target.tagName !== 'INPUT' && e.target.tagName !== 'TEXTAREA') e.preventDefault();\n    });\n    ```\n  - Block `selectstart` (drag text highlighting) outside input/textarea:\n    ```javascript\n    document.addEventListener('selectstart', e => {\n      if (e.target.tagName !== 'INPUT' && e.target.tagName !== 'TEXTAREA') e.preventDefault();\n    });\n    ```\n  - Block `copy` events outside input/textarea:\n    ```javascript\n    document.addEventListener('copy', e => {\n      if (e.target.tagName !== 'INPUT' && e.target.tagName !== 'TEXTAREA') e.preventDefault();\n    });\n    ```\n  - Block keyboard `Ctrl+A` / `Cmd+A` and `Ctrl+C` / `Cmd+C` outside input/textarea:\n    ```javascript\n    document.addEventListener('keydown', e => {\n      const k = e.key.toLowerCase();\n      if ((e.ctrlKey || e.metaKey) && (k === 'a' || k === 'c')) {\n        if (e.target.tagName !== 'INPUT' && e.target.tagName !== 'TEXTAREA') {\n          e.preventDefault();\n        }\n      }\n    });\n    ```\n\n### 2.3 [HISTORY.md](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/HISTORY.md)\n- Append Non-Major Patch 1.0.10 documenting the button label renaming and the mobile/desktop long-press selection prevention rules with reasons.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Dependency & Ripple Effect Analysis\n\n| Component / Flow | Direct / Indirect Dependency | Potential Risk | Mitigation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Student Name/Section Input | Depends on user interaction | If global `user-select: none` covers inputs, students cannot edit or fix typos in their names. | Explicitly set `input, textarea { -webkit-user-select: auto; user-select: auto; }` and exempt `INPUT` and `TEXTAREA` tags from event cancellation. |\n| Choice Selection Buttons (`.opt`) | Click/tap selection during exam | Event handlers might interfere with button click registration. | `contextmenu`, `selectstart`, `copy`, and `keydown` interception do not intercept standard `click` or `pointerup` events. |\n| Result Code Copy (`#cp`) | Copies base64 string to clipboard | Copy blocker might prevent clipboard copy. | `navigator.clipboard.writeText` bypasses document copy events, and manual fallback uses `#codebox` textarea which is explicitly exempted. |\n| Teacher Template Download | `teacher.html` fetches `quizzes/template` | Downloaded file might have outdated code if Firestore template is not re-synced. | Re-sync Firestore `quizzes/template` after updating `index.html`. |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Verification Plan (Rules 3 & 10)\n\n1. **Teacher Button Label Verification**:\n   - Verify `teacher.html` renders `Download Quiz File` in DOM.\n   - Verify clicking `Download Quiz File` successfully triggers downloading `index.html`.\n\n2. **Long-Press & Selection Blocking Verification**:\n   - In `index.html`, trigger simulated long press (`contextmenu`), text selection attempt (`selectstart`), and `Ctrl+A` keydown on question cards, instructions, and options. Verify `defaultPrevented === true`.\n   - On `#name` and `#sec` input fields, simulate text selection and `Ctrl+A`. Verify `defaultPrevented === false` (editing remains fully functional).\n\n3. **Zero In-Code Comments Audit (Rule 9)**:\n   - Run automated scan across all modified files to ensure zero comments, docstrings, or TODOs.\n\n4. **Firestore Template Synchronization**:\n   - Verify `quizzes/template` in Firestore matches the updated `index.html`.\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\CxAdmin\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a\\implementation_plan.md"}}]}
